-- title:
--   Frobenius acts as U_λ modulo monodromy on the eigenplane
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense: $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices and the usual recursions at prime powers, separately for primes dividing and not dividing $M$) and for no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ does there exist a normalised eigenform on $\Gamma_0(M')$ whose coefficients at primes not dividing $M$ agree with those of $g$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals containing $\lambda$ and all prime divisors of $M$, with $\lambda\mid M$ and $\lambda^2\nmid M$. Let $O'$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal, let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 (S \ {lam})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid M$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid M$) with index outside $S\setminus\{\lambda\}$ — to $\mathbb C$ satisfying $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for all such $\ell$, and let $\iota$ map the range of $\chi_g$ into $O'$. Let $O''$ be a further characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field, module-finite and local over $O'$ and a $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-algebra, with fraction field $K$. Write $J_0(M)$ for `JZero M`, the degree-zero divisor class group of the level-$M$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with its Hecke module structure `heckeModuleBar`, and $T=$ [`TateModule lam (JZero M)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15), the module of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda x_{n+1}=x_n$. Assume given: a $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ acting on the $n$-th coordinate through $\mathbb Z/\lambda^n$; a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T)$ induced by the coordinatewise Galois action; a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14) $=\mathbb Z[X_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ to the same endomorphism ring induced by the Hecke action on $T$; and a $K$-subspace $W\subseteq K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T)$ of dimension $2$, stable under every $\rho_M(\sigma)\otimes K$, on which `heckeGen ℓ` acts by the scalar $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, on which the trace of $\rho_M(\sigma)|_W$ equals that same scalar for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over such an $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $A$, and on which `heckeGen lam` acts by the scalar $\iota(\chi_g(U_\lambda))$. The conclusion: for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\lambda$ in its nonunits, every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ and inducing $x\mapsto x^{\lambda}$ on the residue field of $A$, and every $w\in W$, the element $(\rho_M(\sigma)\otimes K)(w)-\iota(\chi_g(U_\lambda))\,w$ lies in the $K$-span of $\{(\rho_M(\tau)\otimes K)(w')-w' : \tau\in A.\mathrm{inertiaSubgroupIn}\ \mathbb Q,\ w'\in W\}$.
--
--   This is the Deligne–Rapoport description of the reduction of $J_0(M)$ at a prime $\lambda$ exactly dividing $M$, read on the Hecke eigenplane of a $\lambda$-new weight-two form: on the unramified quotient obtained by killing the monodromy span, Frobenius at $\lambda$ acts by the eigenvalue $a_\lambda(g)=\chi_g(U_\lambda)$. It feeds the construction of the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to $g$ together with its ordinary line at $\lambda$, used in the local analysis at $\lambda$ of the Frey curve representation.
